Drift: Graph

Purpose:
  Defines drift detection between .sdd and source code.

DriftTypes:
  STACK_DRIFT:
    .sdd stack differs from source stack
  ARCHITECTURE_DRIFT:
    .sdd architecture differs from source architecture
  TASK_DRIFT:
    .sdd task status differs from source state
  DOC_DRIFT:
    .sdd documentation differs from source
  SECURITY_DRIFT:
    .sdd security controls differ from source
  TEST_DRIFT:
    .sdd test claims differ from source tests
  INFRA_DRIFT:
    .sdd infrastructure differs from source
  DECISION_DRIFT:
    .sdd decisions differ from source implementation

DriftClassification:
  VALID_DRIFT:
    Change was intentional and documented
  UNEXPLAINED_DRIFT:
    Change detected without corresponding task/decision
  UNTRACEABLE_CHANGE:
    Source changed with no task, decision, or workflow

DriftDetection:
  Process:
    .sdd vs SOURCE
      ↓
    COMPARE
      ↓
    DETECT DRIFT
      ↓
    CLASSIFY
      ↓
    REPORT

DriftRules:
  [DR1]  Graph MUST detect all drift types.
  [DR2]  Drift MUST be classified as VALID or UNEXPLAINED.
  [DR3]  Untraceable changes MUST be flagged as UNTRACEABLE_CHANGE.
  [DR4]  Drift MUST NOT be silently ignored.

State: +
  